//? Title: Pearson hashing: actual byte lookup states
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
From accumulator zero, each byte performs h=T[h XOR byte] using a complete
permutation of all256 byte values. A fixed-position single-byte substitution in
equal-length messages must change the result, because every subsequent
fixed-byte transition is bijective. Multiple-byte edits and different-length
strings can collide, and there are only256 possible outputs. The original32-word
cohort is descriptive, not a randomness or cryptographic-quality test. No
external dataset is needed.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

From accumulator zero, each byte performs h=T[h XOR byte] using a complete
permutation of all256 byte values. A fixed-position single-byte substitution in
equal-length messages must change the result, because every subsequent
fixed-byte transition is bijective. Multiple-byte edits and different-length
strings can collide, and there are only256 possible outputs. The original32-word
cohort is descriptive, not a randomness or cryptographic-quality test. No
external dataset is needed.

$$ h_0=0,\qquad h_{i+1}=T[h_i\mathbin{\mathrm{XOR}}b_i]. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pearson_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::pearson_hash_trace("hash");
    std::print("| position | byte | before | XOR index | actual lookup result |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.index, int(r.byte),
                   int(r.before), int(r.table_index), int(r.after));
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual input byte lookups\n{}", t.steps.size()));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual first table index\n{}",
                       int(t.steps.front().table_index)));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0}, std::format("Actual final hash byte\n{}", int(t.hash)));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pearson_tiny.svg");
}
```
